  "split_decision": "Extract the complete concrete stored-element existential wrapper from the independent named-property proof seam. Preserve mixed kernel own-provider schemas and their genuine finiteness-label proof wrappers in exact archives rather than weaken a record, invent a map/universal property or add a missing self-provider import.",
  "review_notes": [
    "Extract only the exact theorem that an already supplied I contains a WittElement W equal to I.index. Keep every original C/J/F/D/W/I parameter, the dependent WittElement type, equality and fully qualified provider call unchanged.",
    "The exact inspected provider proves the existential by its stored I.index and rfl. No index, Witt complex or element is constructed independently of the supplied record. No operator/kernel-cokernel formula is inferred.",
    "The other theorem genuinely forwards I.representsOperatorIndex, a separately chosen proposition/proof field with no defining relation to the operator and stored element. Preserve it byte-exact in both archives.",
    "All original import and historical provider identities stay explicit and unreplayed. The source uses the Research site/topology/sheaf-spectrum context, which is distinct from the crystalline Dirac context of the kernel sources; no alias or provider substitution is introduced."
  ],
